.TH PYCECCLIENT "1" "August 2026" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pyCecClient \- demo client for the libCEC Python bindings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pyCecClient
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pyCecClient
is the example program shipped with the Python bindings for libCEC. It
opens a connection to the first CEC adapter it detects, registers itself
on the HDMI CEC bus as a recording device named \fIpyLibCec\fR, and then
reads commands from standard input until told to quit.
.PP
It takes no command line arguments and has no configuration file. It
exists to demonstrate the
.B cec
Python module and to serve as a starting point for scripts of your own;
for day to day use of a CEC adapter see
.BR cec\-client (1),
which offers rather more.
.PP
All libCEC log messages at level
.I traffic
and above are printed as they arrive, as are key presses and incoming CEC
commands.
.SH COMMANDS
Commands are typed at the \fBEnter command:\fR prompt and are case
insensitive.
.TP
.B self
List the logical addresses libCEC has claimed on the bus. The active
source, if it is one of them, is marked with an asterisk.
.TP
.BR as ", " activesource
Broadcast an active source message, making this device the active source.
.TP
.B standby
Put all devices on the bus into standby.
.TP
.B scan
Scan the bus and print, for every device found, its logical and physical
address, vendor, CEC version, OSD name, power status, and whether it is
the active source.
.TP
.BI tx " bytes"
Transmit a raw CEC frame.
.I bytes
is a colon separated list of hexadecimal octets, the first of which
carries the source and destination logical addresses, for example
.B tx 10:04
to send an image view on to the TV.
.TP
.BR q ", " quit
Exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B pyCecClient
exits 0 once the command loop ends. It also exits 0 when no adapter is
found or when the adapter cannot be opened, printing a diagnostic first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/python3/dist\-packages/cec.py
The Python bindings this program demonstrates, provided by the
.B python3\-libcec
package.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cec\-client (1)
.PP
The libCEC API documentation is published at
.UR https://pulse\-eight.github.io/libcec/
.UE .
